Entrance development, hydraulic diameter and section shape (@fd-entrances: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18", #source "../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Mechanics-MIT-2-25.lingua#r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ", #source "../sources/Mecanica-dos-Fluidos-e-Transportes-Gobbi-Dias.lingua#r_1F9KHVCP86X68RR7DTZASE5F1J", #fluid-dynamics "Pipe-resistance-roughness-and-Darcy-versus-Fanning.lingua#r_4428A6CTA9J8GD9VSXPVJTHKBD") { r_2ZV9PF833DSR5B56KY11SZ86A0
**Read:** [Lectures in Elementary Fluid Dynamics — James M. McDonough](../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18), complete internal-flow and entrance treatment; [Advanced Fluid Mechanics — MIT 2.25, Fall 2013](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Mechanics-MIT-2-25.lingua#r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ), developing viscous-flow problems; [Introdução à Mecânica dos Fluidos e aos Fenômenos de Transporte — Gobbi and colleagues](../sources/Mecanica-dos-Fluidos-e-Transportes-Gobbi-Dias.lingua#r_1F9KHVCP86X68RR7DTZASE5F1J), boundary conditions and differential balances.

A nominally uniform inlet profile develops wall layers as it enters a duct. Fully developed flow means that the dimensionless axial profile no longer changes downstream under the stated steady geometry and properties; it does not mean zero velocity gradient everywhere. Pressure and velocity must supply the wall shear and any developing momentum flux.

Define hydraulic diameter as four times flow area divided by wetted perimeter. It is a geometric scale, not proof that every noncircular duct obeys the circular laminar friction law. Solve or consult the exact shape-dependent solution for a rectangular or annular passage and compare profile, flux and wall stress with the circular case.

Estimate the developing length for the actual flow class using a cited correlation and then test its applicability. Distinguish momentum development from thermal or concentration development. Place measurement sections and computational boundaries so that the interpretation of a pressure gradient does not silently mix entrance losses, fully developed resistance and local disturbances.

**Continue:** [Pipe resistance, roughness and Darcy versus Fanning](Pipe-resistance-roughness-and-Darcy-versus-Fanning.lingua#r_4428A6CTA9J8GD9VSXPVJTHKBD).

